Subject: [PATCH] Repetitions: a cut leaving an element keeps its item N frame

A repetition numbered an element's error with `item N` only when it
backtracked; a cut inside the element (`"{" => digit+ "}"`) took the
`Err(e) => return Err(e)` arm and lost the index, so a list element that
failed after its cut could not be told from the others. The arms of
repeat_recording_bounded, repeat_counting_bounded and fold_loop now number
a Cut with the same index (the fold after `stopped`, as before) and return
it as a Cut; the streamed fold numbers a Fail::Cut in its item loop and in
the diagnosing attempt where the item index is known. record, priorities
and the rendered form are unchanged; a parse that succeeds runs the same
code. tests/cut_test.rs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
